# Build output
/denyfirst
/dist/
/bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Coverage
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Go workspace files — machine-specific, must not be shared
go.work
go.work.sum

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Push protection is the real defence; this is the layer before it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
id_ecdsa
*_rsa
*_ed25519
credentials.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
.netrc
.npmrc

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local agent settings.
#
# CLAUDE.md is committed and is project rules everybody shares. Permissions
# are not: an allow list of shell commands in a public repository is a line a
# pull request can add to, and a reviewer reads the code rather than the
# settings. Keep them local and unshared.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local scratch — a place to put things that must never be committed
/tmp/
/scratch/
/local/
# Local counter file. Real deployments name their own path.
#
# The temporary is a pattern rather than one name: each write makes its own,
# so that a periodic write racing a shutdown write cannot land in the same
# file. The entries below this block used to be repeated verbatim, which is
# how a list stops being read.
stats.json
stats.json*.tmp

# ── Logs pulled down for diagnosis ───────────────────────────────────
# `gh run view --log` writes into whatever directory it is run from, and that
# is usually this one. On 2026-08-31 two of them were swept into a commit by
# `git add -A` and reached main. Nothing in those two was sensitive — a public
# workflow log of a public repository, already readable through the API — but
# they are not part of this project, and the next log somebody pulls down
# might come from somewhere less harmless.
#
# The record of an incident belongs in the invariant that came out of it and
# in the comment beside the code it changed, where a reader will find it.
# A raw CI log committed to the source tree is not that.
*.log

# ── Patches applied by hand ──────────────────────────────────────────
# A change arriving as a patch file is applied from wherever it was
# downloaded, and on 2026-09-01 one was downloaded into this directory and
# swept into its own commit by `git add -A` — the same shape as the logs
# above, two days later. Nothing in it was sensitive: it was a diff of this
# repository's own source, public the moment it merged.
#
# The lasting fix is in docs/releasing.md, which no longer tells anybody to
# stage with `git add -A`. This is the layer under it.
*.patch
*.diff
